            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Setting Up",
            "text": "<p><strong>Assembling the Lower Handle</strong><br/>1. Insert the left and right lower handles into the slots of the mower housing. Ensure the locking pin button is secured into place.<br/><br/><strong>Assembling the Upper Handle</strong><br/><br/>1. Fit the upper handle and lower handles together with the wing knobs on both sides of the handle assembly. <br/>2. Secure the cable against the handle frame with the supplied cable clips.<br/>3. When the two wing knobs are loosened, the handle can be folded for easy storage. </p><p>Ensure the power cable is not caught between the folding sections.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Assembling the Grass Collection Bag </strong><br/><br/>Your mower comes with a tool free grass collection bag.<br/>1. Insert the grass collection bag handle into the slots on the upper cover of grass collection bag. Ensure this securely 'clicks’ into place.<br/>2. Secure the metal support rods into the fixing position on either side of the grass collection base.<br/><br/>3. There is a hole in the bottom of the grass collection bag to hang it up if required.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Inserting the Battery Pack<br/></strong><br/>1. Make sure the battery is fully charged.<br/>2. Lift the battery compartment cover on the lawnmower deck.<br/>3. Align the support rails located within the battery compartment with the guides in the battery pack, and then insert the battery pack into the compartment.<br/>4. Push the battery pack until you hear a “click”.<br/>5. Insert the isolator key into the keyholes located within the battery compartment.<br/>6. Close the battery compartment cover.</p><p></p><p>NOTE: The LawnMaster MX 24V 34cm cordless lawn mower is also supplied with a mulching plug for when you want to deposit grass clippings back onto the lawn, rather than collect in the grass bag. <strong>The mulching plug must be removed if collection bag is used during mowing operation</strong>.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Installing the mulching plug</strong></p><p>1. Lift the deflector guard and detach the grass collection bag.<br/>2. Lift and hold the deflector guard up with one hand.<br/>3. With other hand grasp the mulching plug by its upright handle and insert the plug into the rear discharge chute. Ensure that the locking latch snaps into place.<br/>4. Release the deflector guard back into position during operation.<br/></p>",
